      "rationale": "L1 and L2 (same paper, same construct) explicitly state the HA tag was inserted between aa 544 and aa 545 of full-length SLC4A11. Python confirms aa 544 = P and aa 545 = T, both within the extracellular span 489\u2013557. The junction is 56 residues from the upstream TM boundary (477\u2013488) and 13 residues from the downstream TM boundary (558\u2013575), well clear of the \u22653-residue minimum on both sides. L1 is used as the primary supporting clip; L2 is a redundant description of the identical experiment. Full-length BTR1/SLC4A11 expressed in mammalian cells (PBM-SLC4A11 plasmid); HA tag inserted between aa 544 and aa 545, described as a flexible extracellular loop, to assess plasma membrane expression of wild-type and disease-associated mutant constructs.",
